<div class="module">
  <h2>Help</h2>
  <div class="body">

    <h3>Put it on your phone</h3>
    <p><b>iPhone / iPad:</b> open the site in <b>Safari</b> (not Chrome), tap the Share button, then
      <i>Add to Home Screen</i>. Open it from the home-screen icon after that &mdash; it runs full screen,
      and notifications only work from there.</p>
    <p><b>Android:</b> open in Chrome, tap the ⋮ menu, then <i>Install app</i>.</p>
    <p>Then go to <a href="/settings">Settings</a> and turn on notifications.</p>

    <h3>Your profile song</h3>
    <p>Go to <a href="/edit/song">Edit Profile &rarr; Profile Song</a> and upload an audio file (MP3, M4A, OGG,
      WAV, FLAC). It plays when someone opens your page.</p>
    <p>Browsers block autoplay until the visitor has interacted with the page, so on a fresh tab the player
      shows a Play button and starts the moment they tap anywhere. Nothing you can do about that &mdash;
      it is the browser, not the site.</p>
    <p>A pasted link only works if it points straight at an audio file. A YouTube or Spotify page will not play.</p>

    <h3>Wallpaper and layout</h3>
    <p><a href="/edit/design">Edit Profile &rarr; Design</a> covers backgrounds, colours, fonts, cursors and
      a raw CSS box.</p>
    <p>Two things worth knowing:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your wallpaper is applied to the whole page, like it was in 2005.</li>
      <li>Your custom CSS is automatically scoped to your profile area. A broken rule can wreck your own page
        but cannot break the navigation, so you can always get back to the editor and fix it. Old MySpace layout
        codes that start with <code>body { }</code> get rewritten to point at your profile shell, so most of them
        still do roughly the right thing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Turn <b>box transparency</b> down if you want the wallpaper showing through the content boxes.</p>

    <h3>Top 8 &mdash; or Top anything</h3>
    <p><a href="/edit/top">Edit Profile &rarr; Top Friends</a>. Set the count to any number from 0 to 64 and
      choose how many appear per row. Drag to reorder, or use the ▲▼ buttons on a phone.</p>
    <p>Empty slots fill themselves with whoever was online most recently, so the grid never looks half-dead.
      Set the count to 0 to hide the section.</p>

    <h3>HTML in posts</h3>
    <p>About Me, blurbs, comments, blogs, bulletins and mail all accept HTML: tables, fonts, images,
      <code>&lt;marquee&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;blink&gt;</code>, the lot. Scripts, iframes and event handlers
      are stripped on save.</p>

    <h3>Mail vs IM</h3>
    <p><a href="/mail">Mail</a> is for long things and keeps a record. <a href="/im">IM</a> is live chat,
      one-to-one or group, and updates in real time. Both can notify your phone.</p>

    <h3>Something is broken</h3>
    <p>Message <a href="/u/tom">Tom</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

